WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.233
A coding agent thinks in full sentences, and shows you almost none of them.

2
00:00:05.573 --> 00:00:08.539
Reezyn reads that thinking, and says it out loud.

3
00:00:09.489 --> 00:00:13.836
Agents fire tool calls in bursts. Reezyn waits for the pause,

4
00:00:13.836 --> 00:00:17.081
keeps the one thought worth hearing, and drops the backlog.

5
00:00:18.031 --> 00:00:22.550
Every event takes the same path. An adapter reads the session log,

6
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.024
the coalescer picks the burst, the cleaner strips the code, and

7
00:00:26.024 --> 00:00:27.962
Kokoro speaks it locally.

8
00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:31.890
Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, Cursor, OpenCode and

9
00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:37.339
Freebuff are watched directly. Anything else can emit an event of its own.

10
00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:41.965
Code is stripped, paths go, and snake case becomes words.

11
00:00:42.305 --> 00:00:46.577
A technical shorthand is spelled out, two sentences at most are kept, and

12
00:00:46.577 --> 00:00:50.447
if there is no reasoning at all, it names the file instead.

13
00:00:51.397 --> 00:00:54.827
Nine voices, three paces, and language packs for English,

14
00:00:54.827 --> 00:00:59.713
Spanish and French. A pack frames the agent's words in its own

15
00:00:59.713 --> 00:01:02.901
language, but it pronounces them, it does not translate them.

16
00:01:03.851 --> 00:01:07.172
The seedling in the menu bar is the interface:

17
00:01:07.172 --> 00:01:10.692
pause, skip, the last six lines, and a recap of the session.

18
00:01:11.032 --> 00:01:14.251
The CC viewer floats the current line over your

19
00:01:14.251 --> 00:01:17.241
editor, and ignores the pointer until you hold Option.

20
00:01:18.191 --> 00:01:21.223
Each project keeps a small ledger of what you

21
00:01:21.223 --> 00:01:25.156
asked and what the agent concluded. Ask something you already settled, and

22
00:01:25.156 --> 00:01:29.087
Reezyn quotes the earlier answer first, once per prompt,

23
00:01:29.087 --> 00:01:31.508
and at most once every ninety seconds.

24
00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:36.964
Say Reezyn, and dictate. It types the draft and never submits it.

25
00:01:37.304 --> 00:01:40.235
Ready to send it, unless you end with send it now.

26
00:01:40.575 --> 00:01:44.701
When a turn ends, it speaks the answer and reopens the microphone.

27
00:01:45.651 --> 00:01:51.296
Remote access publishes the same session to your phone, over Tailscale, and nowhere else.

28
00:01:51.636 --> 00:01:55.360
Live lines, allow and deny, replies by text or

29
00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.111
voice, read aloud, and a recap.

30
00:01:58.061 --> 00:02:01.440
No cloud calls, no telemetry, no summary model.

31
00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.900
Updates are checked against a checksum and

32
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.797
the same Developer ID before a single byte is swapped in.

33
00:02:08.747 --> 00:02:12.406
Reezyn is free and open source, and installs in a minute.

34
00:02:12.746 --> 00:02:14.103
Then it just talks.
